# A fair coin conditioned on heads: the conditional expectation of c (cwp, the default) is
# wp(S, c) / wlp(S, 1) = (1/2) / (1/2) = 1, so the upper bound 1 holds.
# Expected: valid.  The reduction asks wp_1(S, c) <= 1, where a run blocked by the
# observation is worth the bound 1: 1/2 * 1 + 1/2 * 1 = 1.
nat c;
{
	c := 1;
}[1/2]{
	c := 0;
}
observe(c = 1);
?Ex [c] <= 1
